WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:05.720
SCP-1730 is one of the biggest threats the
Foundation has ever faced.

00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:08.109
SCP-1730 does not exist.

00:00:08.109 --> 00:00:10.679
It was June 5th when the compound was first
discovered.

00:00:10.679 --> 00:00:15.499
A large complex of structures in rural Texas,
about fifteen kilometers northwest of the

00:00:15.499 --> 00:00:16.960
Mexican border.

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:21.470
Located in Big Bend Ranch State Park, it was
easily the biggest structure in the area.

00:00:21.470 --> 00:00:25.030
But there was no record of any such structure
ever being built.

00:00:25.030 --> 00:00:31.539
A massive network of power stations, containment
facilities, and research buildings, SCP-1730

00:00:31.539 --> 00:00:33.940
looked like it had been abandoned for a long
time.

00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:36.950
The exterior was degraded, but the building
was still operating.

00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:41.170
A power generator had been running for an
indeterminate amount of time, even as the

00:00:41.170 --> 00:00:42.789
infrastructure degraded.

00:00:42.789 --> 00:00:45.829
Power flickered through the sight and fuel
leaked frequently.

00:00:45.829 --> 00:00:50.190
But there was one detail that attracted the
attention of SCP brass.

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:56.100
SCP-1730 bore identifying markings linking
it to Foundation Site 13, a research facility

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:59.070
that was marked for construction near Nome,
Alaska.

00:00:59.070 --> 00:01:03.660
But Site 13 had never been built, having been
abandoned in the planning stages.

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:08.370
So why is it in the middle of Texas, fully
constructed and long abandoned?

00:01:08.370 --> 00:01:12.000
The Foundation needed to know more, and they
needed their best to investigate.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:14.620
It was time to call in the “Game Wardens”.

00:01:14.620 --> 00:01:19.440
Apollo-3, the mobile task force used to investigate
dangerous sites, was brought in, and five

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:24.630
elite agents were briefed and sent in - Ross,
Houston, Noah, Ohalo, and Vigo.

00:01:24.630 --> 00:01:28.930
It didn’t take long for them to discover
that something was very wrong with the site

00:01:28.930 --> 00:01:30.400
of SCP-1730.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:34.950
The facility was located in the middle of
south Texas - but the local flora surrounding

00:01:34.950 --> 00:01:37.500
it was native to Nome, Alaska.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:42.180
Something had transplanted a building that
shouldn’t exist to another place and time.

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:46.210
Commander Ross ordered his men to enter, with
Houston taking lead, and they discovered that

00:01:46.210 --> 00:01:48.580
entry led down a long staircase.

00:01:48.580 --> 00:01:52.950
They descended slowly, following a strange
light that no one could identify - but had

00:01:52.950 --> 00:01:57.040
a sudden shock when they discovered that the
basement of the staircase was missing.

00:01:57.040 --> 00:02:00.890
The light suddenly stopped, and it became
so dark that it was impossible to see what

00:02:00.890 --> 00:02:02.610
lay beyond the staircase.

00:02:02.610 --> 00:02:07.200
Upon probing the inky black void at the base
of the staircase, they determined it wasn’t

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:09.010
a fog or shadow.

00:02:09.010 --> 00:02:10.010
It was a liquid.

00:02:10.010 --> 00:02:11.450
And it was rising.

00:02:11.450 --> 00:02:14.720
Ross ordered his men back, but Houston was
in too deep.

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:17.430
He couldn’t break free from the inky black
liquid.

00:02:17.430 --> 00:02:21.420
The men pulled him away, and got him free
- but his legs were gone!

00:02:21.420 --> 00:02:23.920
Not ripped off, because there was no blood
anywhere.

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:26.750
Smoothly cut off, as if they were never there.

00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:30.080
And as they put Houston down, he stood up
- on phantom legs.

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:34.860
He didn’t feel any pain, but everyone could
tell something was very wrong with this place.

00:02:34.860 --> 00:02:39.080
And the messages they started seeing on the
wall made clear they weren’t the only ones

00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:40.090
who knew it.

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:41.600
“What Happened to Site 13?”

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:42.600
“Death Here”

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:43.600
“Not My Body”

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:44.600
“Bleed”

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:50.070
There had been other people - or things - inside
SCP-1730, and they wanted anyone who entered

00:02:50.070 --> 00:02:53.220
to know that this was a very dangerous place
to be.

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:56.270
As they advanced down the hall back towards
the entrance, they saw what looked like a

00:02:56.270 --> 00:02:57.770
person in the distance.

00:02:57.770 --> 00:03:01.370
But as they approached, it became clear this
wasn’t another explorer.

00:03:01.370 --> 00:03:06.220
It was an old, horribly disfigured corpse
seemingly attached to the wall.

00:03:06.220 --> 00:03:09.430
Not by chains - but fused into the wall in
unnatural ways.

00:03:09.430 --> 00:03:14.360
At first, the team seemed unconcerned - recognizing
the corpse as someone named Zachary.

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:19.299
Fortunately, command back at base realized
this as the effects of some sort of cognitohazard

00:03:19.299 --> 00:03:21.770
- a mental infection - in the base.

00:03:21.770 --> 00:03:26.410
They uploaded a filter to their helmets, and
the team recoiled in horror at the site in

00:03:26.410 --> 00:03:27.410
front of them.

00:03:27.410 --> 00:03:28.819
But the horrors were just beginning.

00:03:28.819 --> 00:03:32.880
They turned around to see a shimmering, humanoid
entity in the hallway behind them.

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:35.750
As it approached, its footsteps distorted
the hallway around.

00:03:35.750 --> 00:03:41.400
It pulled AP-3 Noah towards it, without touching
him, and as the soldier was pulled into its

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:43.260
clutches, his body started to distort.

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:47.810
Vigo was next, being grabbed by the arm by
a long appendage, and his arm started to change

00:03:47.810 --> 00:03:48.810
color and distort.

00:03:48.810 --> 00:03:52.040
But the foundation sent Apollo-3 in prepared.

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:56.530
Houston produced a portable reality anchor,
designed to handle reality-warping entities,

00:03:56.530 --> 00:03:59.610
and with a flash of red light the creature
was revealed.

00:03:59.610 --> 00:04:04.330
It was a horribly elongated humanoid that
only existed for a second before the reality

00:04:04.330 --> 00:04:07.490
anchor erased it and restored the hallway
to its normal state.

00:04:07.490 --> 00:04:11.260
Vigo would recover, with the strange red color
in his arm fading eventually.

00:04:11.260 --> 00:04:13.180
Noah wasn’t so lucky.

00:04:13.180 --> 00:04:14.590
He was already dead.

00:04:14.590 --> 00:04:18.220
And had been fused into the wall just like
the unfortunate corpse.

00:04:18.220 --> 00:04:22.310
These horrors had been encountered just by
trying to return to the entrance, so it was

00:04:22.310 --> 00:04:27.340
clear the only smart thing to do was to descend
further into the facilities and get some answers.

00:04:27.340 --> 00:04:32.000
As they advanced, not encountering any other
supernatural entities, they saw more evidence

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:34.900
of the dark things that had occurred in Site
13.

00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:39.990
The infirmary had been torn apart, a cafeteria
had been melted into slag, and a large group

00:04:39.990 --> 00:04:44.030
of containment cells ended with a section
called “Olympia Class”.

00:04:44.030 --> 00:04:49.340
But while most of the other cells were standard
sized, these were over 100 meters high.

00:04:49.340 --> 00:04:53.940
What had the foundation - or whoever ran this
place - been keeping in these cells?

00:04:53.940 --> 00:04:58.240
They would get more answers as they made their
way down another hall, where they saw a single

00:04:58.240 --> 00:05:01.250
television still working and illuminating
their hallway.

00:05:01.250 --> 00:05:04.889
At first the television flickered, but the
image soon cleared, and the agents were able

00:05:04.889 --> 00:05:06.470
to see what was broadcasting.

00:05:06.470 --> 00:05:08.390
It was the interior of a containment cell.

00:05:08.390 --> 00:05:09.960
And there was someone in it.

00:05:09.960 --> 00:05:14.931
And they recognized them as one of the most
dangerous beings contained by the SCP Foundation

00:05:14.931 --> 00:05:16.030
- Bobble the Clown.

00:05:16.030 --> 00:05:22.050
A predatory supernatural clown that inhabits
a children’s TV show, Bobble the Clown was

00:05:22.050 --> 00:05:26.910
broadcast by an unknown source and could only
be seen by children under ten.

00:05:26.910 --> 00:05:31.139
Originally seeming to be a normal kids’
show about a clown, every episode eventually

00:05:31.139 --> 00:05:35.870
devolved into the murderous Bobble teaching
the kids how to do horrible things like arson

00:05:35.870 --> 00:05:36.870
or torture.

00:05:36.870 --> 00:05:40.870
The Foundation eventually captured and isolated
Bobble’s broadcast, but the clown remained

00:05:40.870 --> 00:05:42.730
hostile and vicious.

00:05:42.730 --> 00:05:43.730
Not here.

00:05:43.730 --> 00:05:48.300
As the team talked to the Bobble trapped in
the mysterious Site 13, it became clear that

00:05:48.300 --> 00:05:51.450
this clown was broken by whatever it had experienced.

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:55.630
It rambled, it hid from the camera, and it
was clearly terrified as it told the team

00:05:55.630 --> 00:05:57.050
about the horrors of the site.

00:05:57.050 --> 00:06:01.340
And it seemed to recognize the agents as something
familiar - but not completely familiar.

00:06:01.340 --> 00:06:05.340
It claimed to be able to smell them - and
said they smelled different.

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:09.820
As Bobble rambled on and on, the agents learned
about a man named Emerson, who ran the site.

00:06:09.820 --> 00:06:13.680
Like the Foundation, he was obsessed with
containing the strange and dangerous entities

00:06:13.680 --> 00:06:14.680
in the world.

00:06:14.680 --> 00:06:18.120
But unlike the foundation, he didn’t just
want to protect the world from them.

00:06:18.120 --> 00:06:19.320
He hated them.

00:06:19.320 --> 00:06:22.250
The entities in Site 13 didn’t even have
numbers - they might identify by them.

00:06:22.250 --> 00:06:26.770
Emerson wanted to use them up however he wanted
and dispose of them - in something Bobble

00:06:26.770 --> 00:06:28.760
called the “meat grinder”.

00:06:28.760 --> 00:06:32.720
Entities that outlived their usefulness were
taken down below - and none were ever heard

00:06:32.720 --> 00:06:33.729
from again.

00:06:33.729 --> 00:06:38.669
It was directly counter to every SCP Foundation
policy - but this site had clearly been performing

00:06:38.669 --> 00:06:40.650
these horrible experiments for years.

00:06:40.650 --> 00:06:41.650
How?

00:06:41.650 --> 00:06:42.900
And why hadn’t anyone ever heard of it?

00:06:42.900 --> 00:06:47.080
The team continued to make their way into
the facility, but their signals were lost

00:06:47.080 --> 00:06:48.960
as they entered the cryogenics unit.

00:06:48.960 --> 00:06:52.550
By the time contact had been restored, they
were no longer alone.

00:06:52.550 --> 00:06:53.550
There were survivors.

00:06:53.550 --> 00:06:56.850
Both agents of the foundation - and survivors
of the facility.

00:06:56.850 --> 00:06:58.699
And they were angry.

00:06:58.699 --> 00:07:02.370
With no way out and massively outnumbered,
they called for backup.

00:07:02.370 --> 00:07:07.470
Mobile Task Force T-5, also known as “Samsara”,
was reserved for the heavy-duty missions.

00:07:07.470 --> 00:07:12.330
They’re an elite group of practically immortal
cyborgs fashioned from the flesh of a god,

00:07:12.330 --> 00:07:17.520
and equipped with further cybernetic enhancements
to eliminate Keter-level threats and to protect

00:07:17.520 --> 00:07:19.350
themselves from cognitohazards.

00:07:19.350 --> 00:07:23.490
They were sent in through a drainage gate
to look for survivors and neutralize whatever

00:07:23.490 --> 00:07:24.490
lay within.

00:07:24.490 --> 00:07:28.290
They didn’t know what to expect, but they
knew one thing - no one who had been sent

00:07:28.290 --> 00:07:29.669
in had come out.

00:07:29.669 --> 00:07:32.950
It wasn’t long before they realized how
dangerous this mission would be.

00:07:32.950 --> 00:07:37.380
As they came across some large gated drainage
pipes, they could see at least twenty charred

00:07:37.380 --> 00:07:42.009
bodies of humanoids pushed up against the
gate, some reaching their hands through.

00:07:42.009 --> 00:07:46.770
Whatever had happened in Site 13, these unfortunate
beings had been desperate to escape.

00:07:46.770 --> 00:07:50.669
As they made their way down the drainage pipe,
they could feel it getting hotter, as if they

00:07:50.669 --> 00:07:52.020
were nearing an energy source.

00:07:52.020 --> 00:07:54.919
And there was one other odd thing about the
pipe.

00:07:54.919 --> 00:07:57.100
It was draining inward, not out.

00:07:57.100 --> 00:08:01.690
They made their way to a control room, where
many of the consoles had been destroyed.

00:08:01.690 --> 00:08:05.150
Looking through a window, their view was obscured
by a mysterious black mass.

00:08:05.150 --> 00:08:09.660
On the control panels, they could read terms
like “incinerator” and “body pit access”.

00:08:09.660 --> 00:08:13.699
They split up, trying to find answers, but
found many of their accesses blocked by the

00:08:13.699 --> 00:08:14.820
black mass.

00:08:14.820 --> 00:08:19.449
As the T-5 task force argued over their next
move, they were startled by a sudden jolt.

00:08:19.449 --> 00:08:21.680
The giant mass had started moving.

00:08:21.680 --> 00:08:26.520
The team watched as the mass spun, revealing
a giant turbine, which turned the inky substance

00:08:26.520 --> 00:08:30.710
into a fine slurry that was then scorched
by giant streaks of fire.

00:08:30.710 --> 00:08:35.180
One of T-5 shot open the glass chamber, allowing
the team to get closer - and blasting them

00:08:35.180 --> 00:08:36.490
with a wave of heat.

00:08:36.490 --> 00:08:40.999
As they descended into the chamber, they could
see a massive plant-like structure overhead,

00:08:40.999 --> 00:08:42.159
which started to shake.

00:08:42.159 --> 00:08:47.209
Suddenly, thousands of glowing pods were released
from the massive plant, and each one lit up

00:08:47.209 --> 00:08:49.679
and let the team view the chamber more clearly.

00:08:49.679 --> 00:08:53.180
But it was what was inside the pods that was
more disturbing.

00:08:53.180 --> 00:08:58.149
Each pod had a humanoid shape inside, seemingly
reaching towards the team, until they hit

00:08:58.149 --> 00:09:00.680
the slurry below - and the shadows went dark.

00:09:00.680 --> 00:09:04.699
The team descended to investigate the slurry,
when something started to leak out of the

00:09:04.699 --> 00:09:05.699
walls.

00:09:05.699 --> 00:09:07.399
Looking at it, they could see something moving
within.

00:09:07.399 --> 00:09:11.420
One of the team members picked the wriggling
object out of the black liquid - and it took

00:09:11.420 --> 00:09:12.720
a bite out of his hand!

00:09:12.720 --> 00:09:16.870
It was a leech - and there were thousands
more of them moving towards the slurry, consuming

00:09:16.870 --> 00:09:17.870
it.

00:09:17.870 --> 00:09:19.420
And as the leeches ate, they started growing.

00:09:19.420 --> 00:09:24.179
They seemed to be moving in unison, communicating
with a larger being lurking at the base of

00:09:24.179 --> 00:09:25.179
the slurry.

00:09:25.179 --> 00:09:26.879
A larger leech, a queen?

00:09:26.879 --> 00:09:27.879
Or something else?

00:09:27.879 --> 00:09:30.480
The team wasn’t sticking around to find
out.

00:09:30.480 --> 00:09:34.889
They beat a hurried escape from the leech
room, finding themselves in another hallway.

00:09:34.889 --> 00:09:39.240
Whatever the black substance was, the entities
who had been here had used it, scrawling “Blood”

00:09:39.240 --> 00:09:41.269
on the walls over and over again.

00:09:41.269 --> 00:09:44.899
Occasionally, they would come across a drained
corpse covered in the black fluid.

00:09:44.899 --> 00:09:46.779
Had the leeches bled them dry?

00:09:46.779 --> 00:09:50.649
The facility was so sprawling that the team
knew that if they wanted any chance of navigating

00:09:50.649 --> 00:09:53.369
it safely, they needed to get the lay of the
land.

00:09:53.369 --> 00:09:55.180
They needed to find the control center.

00:09:55.180 --> 00:09:58.869
The door read “Stairs to Cryonics” and
the leeches were nowhere to be found.

00:09:58.869 --> 00:10:00.540
It seemed like a safe path.

00:10:00.540 --> 00:10:04.570
But as soon as the team entered, the temperature
dropped drastically, to well below where it

00:10:04.570 --> 00:10:05.940
would be safe for a human to survive.

00:10:05.940 --> 00:10:10.230
The team’s internal heating system kicked
in, saving their lives, but that wasn’t

00:10:10.230 --> 00:10:11.230
the only threat.

00:10:11.230 --> 00:10:15.389
The team was about to encounter exactly what
Site 13 was keeping locked up.

00:10:15.389 --> 00:10:18.709
As soon as they entered the room, sound ceased
to work.

00:10:18.709 --> 00:10:22.939
The filters in their gear were overloaded,
and the team saw warnings around the room.

00:10:22.939 --> 00:10:23.939
“Silence”

00:10:23.939 --> 00:10:24.939
“Don’t Look”

00:10:24.939 --> 00:10:29.290
A massive, multi-limbed figure emerged, with
each of its sixty arms moving independently.

00:10:29.290 --> 00:10:34.589
The creature had no head, but a large circular
structure covered with ancient glowing symbols.

00:10:34.589 --> 00:10:38.139
Whatever it was, it was ancient, all-powerful
- and deadly.

00:10:38.139 --> 00:10:42.019
The team scrambled to get away, as the glyphs
on the creature burned white hot.

00:10:42.019 --> 00:10:43.639
Anyone who touched it was burned.

00:10:43.639 --> 00:10:47.249
Anyone who looked too long at it felt their
optical implants burn out.

00:10:47.249 --> 00:10:52.420
The symbols on the creature were indecipherable,
but one word was clear and printed in English.

00:10:52.420 --> 00:10:53.420
“EMERSON”

00:10:53.420 --> 00:10:58.350
Site 13 was from another world, another timeline
where the SCP foundation evolved into something

00:10:58.350 --> 00:10:59.350
horrible.

00:10:59.350 --> 00:11:03.459
Ruled over by Elliott Emerson, it tortured
its captured beings, and eventually killed

00:11:03.459 --> 00:11:05.610
most of them in the horrors of the incinerators.

00:11:05.610 --> 00:11:10.720
When an escape threatened to destroy the facility,
Emerson successfully activated a device that

00:11:10.720 --> 00:11:13.300
removed the facility from their world - into
ours.

00:11:13.300 --> 00:11:17.579
Of course, as any avid follower of the SCP
Foundation will know, there’s far more to

00:11:17.579 --> 00:11:18.699
the story than this.

00:11:18.699 --> 00:11:23.339
Emerson may have been the start of Site 13’s
problems, but he was far from the end.

00:11:23.339 --> 00:11:27.850
We’re talking about a tale so epic in size
and scope that it wouldn’t be possible to

00:11:27.850 --> 00:11:33.199
fit it into one video - A tale of subterranean
horror, a daring rescue mission into the bowels

00:11:33.199 --> 00:11:36.550
of Site 13, and an anomalous battle to end
all battles.

00:11:36.550 --> 00:11:41.160
And you can look forward to that epic tale
- including the horrifying story of leech

00:11:41.160 --> 00:11:46.829
boy, and the tragic saga of Dr. Hadley - in
part two: The Samsara Extraction Mission.

00:11:46.829 --> 00:11:48.790
Trust us - it’s worth waiting up for.

